list.item:
—exchange of information by all means available in the event of an
                        unauthorized missile launch or other acts that could lead to the use of
                        nuclear weapons;

—mutual exchange of information on detection of unidentified objects by
                        early warning systems, or notification of signs of interference with these
                        warning systems or with corresponding communications facilities;

—notification of planned missile launches to points beyond national
                        territories (the Soviets announce their tests to the Pacific, but not tests
                        to Kamchatka);
